ion_dragview\/accessibilityrotor(_:entries:)-5jrrv","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityRotor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"AccessibilitySystemRotor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI24AccessibilitySystemRotorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"entries","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[],"title":"accessibilityRotor(_:entries:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityRotor(_:entries:)-5jrrv"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"role":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"role":"collection","title":"Swami","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}]}}}